#NEXUS

[ dalman2025a_fig32: Large rectangular tree in a page render; the coloured tip names are printed over the ends of the branches and touch neighbouring names. Polytomies: Tethyshadros-Telmatosaurus-Lophorhothon-Fylax with Hadrosauridae (five), Brachylophosaurini (five), the four-way node in Lambeosaurini, and Kritosaurini (five). Hadrosauridae, Lambeosaurinae and Saurolophinae are printed with leader lines; the tribes are circled letters keyed in the 'Taxonomy' box (T Tsintaosaurini, C Corythosauria, P Parasaurolophini, L Lambeosaurini, B Brachylophosaurini, E Edmontosaurini, S Saurolophini, K Kritosaurini) and are kept on their nodes. Bremer and bootstrap values are not encoded; a silhouette and the 'Biogeography' and 'Taxonomy' boxes sit at the left and right. 84 tips, 4 polytomies (5, 4, 5, 5 children); 11 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

